amming language  but you know thank thankfully for this  ignorant because it led me to start this  project so Noor is an imperative algo  based programming language that I  created specifically thinking about  myself is it that was the little kid if  I was you know high school or middle  schooler  you know what would like be natural for  me to learn and this is a sample program  in noir I think you know I'll tell what  this program does but in case you can't  we'll walk through it anyways and so the  first line in this program says the coup  de chelly v1 to 100 which basically  means that you know for each thing in  the range of 1 to 100  and then the second line is check take  the number in the for loop and then  check if it's mod get them all three  value of it and so there's a function  invocation an assignment expression and  then the third line is just print the  number in the for loop and then the  third thing is check if the mod three is  you know equal to zero if it is is  clearly divisible by three print that  out print or print fizz if it's  divisible by five print buzz and then  the final parts to this you know program  here are the key words a bus which in  Arabic means like the end or the end and  in this for in this program I make a  call to a function here on the second  line and that function is just you know  get the mod with three of the number and  this is a function in nor and so the  function starts off with instruct a  worker you know and I try to make it  like this child like you know silly  language because I want to be like more  natural feeling and then you say you  give it the function name then you give  it the function arguments that it will  take and then you say to do because I'm  like a little kid I kinda want to  understand it as you know tell something  to do these things for me and then you  have the function body and in this case  I take the argument that was passed in  I'm Ottawa three and I store the result  in a variable called done or D and then  I returned that and so that was a you  know fizzbuzz ignore and i won't be able  to get into the internals of how i  created nor but i'll just tell you that  i used tool called Peggy is which  creates a compiler for you and it's a  really nice tool if you want to you know  create your own small DSL you should  check it out but one thing that sort of  came into a question while I was working  on this is how do I go about choosing  keywords and Arabic is like a big  languages you know very there's a lot of  variety to it and there's classical  Arabic there's modern Standard Arabic  and there's my own dialect of Arabic and  if you know if you don't understand it  the trees kind of something like this  and it's an approximation that you have  classical Arabic which is like a really  old Arabic going dating back to the  seventh century and then you have  dialectic Arabic which is what people  use on a day-to-day basis this is well  like me my mom talked with and  have modern Standard Arabic this is what  like official court documents are in  this is what news is in like Al Jazeera  they want to reach a wide audience so  they'll use this very formal Arabic  that's not particular to anybody but for  Noor I especially used my Sudanese  dialect because I was think about myself  is like what would I would like really  get me started on this and just to show  you a map of all these dialects and how  they vary on you know I'm from Sudan and  so this is the area where my dialect is  really prevalent and but you know  there's different dialects across North  Africa in the Middle East and you know  when I never got public some people who  really liked the fact that I use my own  dialect some people you know thought  that I was Egyptian because they're  trying to you know triangulate my where  I'm from based on a few key words and  it's kind of hard to do some people I  thought it was some like the Gulf and  I'm not from the Gulf and some people  really didn't 